Subject: [PATCH] Cabinet link (local events and commands), and menus open on their first game

Cabinet link: with settings.conf "linkEvents = yes" RetroFE tells a helper on the same PC what
is selected and what is started, and takes two commands from it - go to a named game, and open
(what the Select button does). It only ever uses 127.0.0.1 (events to port 47801, commands on
47802), so nothing on the network can drive it; the helper (tools\AmLink) talks to the other
cabinets. Each event says who caused it: user (a menu action was pressed on this cabinet in the
last 3 s), remote (a link command) or auto. Off by default.

Menus open on their first game: on a racing rig, where pedal axes are bound to up / down, up and
down both read as held for about 250 ms after a menu is entered. "Down wins" then moved the list:
Racing opened on its third game. Opposite directions held together now cancel.

"Somebody is here" is a pressed menu action or a real direction, not a raw button event: an
H-shifter left in gear is a held button and reports itself as a press.

Tested on DESKTOP-RACE1 with a stand-in helper: goto and open move and enter menus and start an
entry; Racing opens on 1/91; Down / Up move one game each and are reported as user.
---
